SCHEDULE: {"1":"Cara","2":"Hana","3":"Ann","4":"Ben","5":"Finn","6":"Ivo","7":"Dev","8":"Gus","9":"Elif"}
CONFIDENCE: 99

The "immediately after" rules force two blocks of four: Hana–Ann–Ben–Finn and Ivo–Dev–Gus–Elif. Cara is the ninth person. "Ann before Dev" and "Ben before Gus" put the Hana block first. "Ann and Ivo at least three apart" then requires a gap of at least three slots between Ann and Ivo, which leaves Cara as the only person who can sit before Hana. That puts Cara in slot 1 and fixes the rest. I checked all 15 constraints against this arrangement and each one holds.
